# Optional override for the API root.
#
# Normally you do NOT need this. public/config.json already lists a backend per
# host and is read at run time, so one build works against any of them:
#
#   localhost      -> http://localhost:5100      the API on this machine
#   202.51.3.68    -> http://202.51.3.68:8013    the live server
#
# The key is the first label of the hostname the dashboard is served from, or
# the whole address when that is a bare IP. Deployed to 202.51.3.68 on any port,
# the second entry is picked automatically.
#
# Set this only to point a LOCAL dev server at a different backend — running
# `npm run dev` on localhost against the live API, say. It wins over config.json
# and also forces useMockApi off. Copy to .env.local, which is gitignored.
#
# Whichever backend you choose has to allow this origin in Cors:AllowedOrigins
# on the API, or the browser blocks the call. http://localhost:5000 is already
# in that list.
#
# Note the trailing /api: this value replaces the base URL *and* apiPath.
VITE_API_BASE=http://202.51.3.68:8013/api
